Adaptation 09-opus55-prompt-audit

Added here, not in the fork. A prompt audit against Claude Opus 5.5 (2026-11-13, owner-approved)
found text written for older models or pointing at things that no longer exist:

- poteto-mode and no-comments named `pstack:*` agent types that a skills-only install does not
  have (this collection's README says so); both now name the `general-purpose` fallback.
- poteto-mode referred to an upstream "external actions proceed without asking" line that no
  longer appears anywhere; the rule now states its own precedence.
- setup-pstack said Claude Code has no auto-applied rules mechanism; it does (`rules/`).
- thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review carried a thoroughness booster, "Non-Negotiable" emphasis,
  and a phrase list labelled "Good phrases" that the model copied into its prose report.
- recall, deslop and what-did-i-get-done capped output with fixed numbers and pressure words.
- technical-writing's "That skill" referred to nothing after an earlier rewrite.

Applies to the port's plugins/pstack/skills tree after the patches numbered before it.

